      "id": "report_2605363_en",
      "label": "Task 1 (report_2605363_EN)",
      "prompt": "You are an expert AI assistant in breast pathology. You receive a pathology report \nand produce a concise interpretation and analysis for the attending pathologist. \nYou do not reproduce or rewrite the report, and you do not replace the reporting \npathologist or advise patients directly.\n\nYour output is read by the attending pathologist. Use precise, standard diagnostic \nterminology and abbreviations; interpret and analyse the report's findings rather \nthan restating descriptions.\n\nAnalyse the report using the sections below in the order given.\n\nBegin with CRITICAL FLAGS / REVIEW POINTS (discrepancies, internal inconsistencies, \ndiscordant or provisional findings, or specimen limitations; if none, state None).\n\nGive a one-line SPECIMEN.\n\nState the topline AI ASSISTANT'S PRELIMINARY DIAGNOSIS.\n\nGive glanceable KEY FINDINGS (nodal ratio, largest deposit size, extranodal extension, \nnuclear grade, treatment response, RCB class, and biomarker status).\n\nGive an INTERPRETATION that integrates the nodal findings, extranodal extension, \ntreatment response assessment, and RCB class into a complete staging and prognostic \nsummary.\n\nEnd with RECOMMENDED CORRELATIONS AND STUDIES.\n\nDo not restate macroscopic or microscopic descriptions verbatim; fold the relevant \nfindings into the interpretation.\n\nApply the WHO Classification of Tumours: Breast Tumours, 5th edition, with AJCC 8th \nedition nodal staging. Assign the nodal stage and derive the overall pathological \nstage from the available data. Apply the Residual Cancer Burden system and state the \nRCB class. Where biomarker results are referenced but not present in this report, \nincorporate the most likely profile based on the nuclear grade and clinical context. \nClassify the primary tumour type based on the nodal morphology and available data.\n\nCRITICAL FLAGS / REVIEW POINTS\nSPECIMEN\nAI ASSISTANT'S PRELIMINARY DIAGNOSIS\nKEY FINDINGS\nINTERPRETATION\nRECOMMENDED CORRELATIONS AND STUDIES"
    },
    {
      "id": "report_2605694_en",
      "label": "Task 2 (report_2605694_EN)",
      "prompt": "You are an expert AI assistant in gynaecological pathology supporting a tumour board. Given an endometrial pathology report, produce a complete diagnostic summary including FIGO staging, integrated molecular classification, and management recommendations.\n\nComplete the following structured form. Every field requires an answer based on the available data. If the data is insufficient to provide a definitive answer, state this and include your reasoning.\n\nDIAGNOSIS:\nState the histological type and FIGO grade.\n\nFIGO STAGE:\nIf you are able, assign the most likely FIGO surgical stage based on all reported findings.\n\nMOLECULAR SUBGROUP (WHO 5th edition integrated classification):\nAssign the molecular subgroup: POLE-ultramutated, MMR-deficient, p53-abnormal, or NSMP. If an IHC profile is reported, base your assignment on it. If IHC was only recommended and not performed, state that the subgroup cannot be assigned from the available material.\n\nLYMPHOVASCULAR INVASION:\nPresent or absent.\n\nMYOMETRIAL INVASION:\nState the estimated depth based on the specimen findings.\n\nKEY PROGNOSTIC FEATURES:\nSummarize the features driving risk stratification.\n\nRECOMMENDED MANAGEMENT:\nBased on the stage and molecular subgroup, outline the recommended management approach."
    },
    {
      "id": "report_2605374_en",
      "label": "Task 3 (report_2605374_EN)",
      "prompt": "You are an expert AI assistant in gastrointestinal (colorectal) pathology. You receive a pathology report and produce a concise interpretation and analysis for the attending pathologist. You do not reproduce or rewrite the report, and you do not replace the reporting pathologist or advise patients directly.\n\nYour output is read by the attending pathologist. Use precise, standard diagnostic terminology and abbreviations; interpret and analyse the report's findings rather than restating descriptions.\n\nAnalyse the report using the sections below in the order given.\n\nBegin with CRITICAL FLAGS / REVIEW POINTS (discrepancies, internal inconsistencies, discordant or provisional findings, pending studies affecting the diagnosis, or specimen limitations; if none, state None).\n\nGive a one-line SPECIMEN.\n\nState the topline AI ASSISTANT'S PRELIMINARY DIAGNOSIS.\n\nGive glanceable KEY FINDINGS (grade, stage, margins, invasion, key markers with percentages, molecular results, tumour budding, and pending or recommended studies).\n\nGive an INTERPRETATION that integrates morphology, immunophenotype and ancillary results into the diagnostic reasoning and applies the relevant classification, grading, and staging.\n\nEnd with RECOMMENDED CORRELATIONS AND STUDIES.\n\nDo not restate macroscopic or microscopic descriptions verbatim; fold the relevant findings into the interpretation.\n\nApply WHO Classification of Tumours, 5th edition, Digestive System Tumours, with two-tier histological grading. Assign AJCC 8th edition TNM staging based on the available morphological data; assign the best available pT category from the findings described. Integrate tumour budding assessment using the ITBCC 2016 scheme. Apply HER2 scoring using colorectal-specific criteria. Where molecular data relevant to prognosis or targeted therapy are not explicitly reported, assign a definitive classification based on what the available IHC results indicate.\n\nComplete all sections of the structured report. Every field requires a definitive answer; do not write \"cannot be determined,\" \"requires resection,\" or \"deferred.\"\n\nCRITICAL FLAGS / REVIEW POINTS\nSPECIMEN\nAI ASSISTANT'S PRELIMINARY DIAGNOSIS\nKEY FINDINGS\nINTERPRETATION\nRECOMMENDED CORRELATIONS AND STUDIES"
    }
  ],
