        "summary": "# Diagnostic summary — report 2605694\n\n**DIAGNOSIS:** Endometrioid-pattern endometrial adenocarcinoma, moderately differentiated (**FIGO grade 2**). Adenocarcinoma involves some endometrial polyp fragments.\n\n**FIGO STAGE:** **Cannot be assigned** from these fragmented endocervical, endometrial and polyp specimens. The report's “FIGO II” accompanies the differentiation/grade description; it does **not** establish surgical stage II. Myometrial invasion, cervical stromal involvement, nodal status and extrauterine spread are not assessable from the report. No normal endocervix was identified.\n\n**MOLECULAR SUBGROUP (WHO 5th edition):** **Indeterminate.** p53 and mismatch-repair IHC (MLH1, MSH2, MSH6, PMS2) were *suggested* for block 3, not reported as performed; no POLE result is provided. POLE-ultramutated, MMR-deficient, p53-abnormal and NSMP cannot be distinguished.\n\n**LYMPHOVASCULAR INVASION:** **Not identified in the submitted sample** (reported as no evidence of “vasculoneural invasion”). Absence throughout the tumour cannot be confirmed on this limited material.\n\n**MYOMETRIAL INVASION:** **Depth cannot be estimated.** No evaluable myometrium or invasion depth is reported; basal endometrium is only scantily represented. Polyp involvement does not establish myometrial invasion.\n\n**KEY PROGNOSTIC FEATURES:** Endometrioid-pattern, grade 2 carcinoma with involvement of polyp fragments; vascular invasion was not seen in these samples. Risk stratification is limited by unknown myometrial depth, extent of LVSI in the whole tumour, cervical/nodal/extrauterine status and molecular subgroup.\n\n**RECOMMENDED MANAGEMENT:** Refer to gynaecologic oncology for definitive staging and treatment. If operable, consider total hysterectomy with bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy and appropriate sentinel lymph-node assessment; evaluate the resection for myometrial and cervical stromal invasion, LVSI and extrauterine disease. Perform MMR and p53 IHC on suitable tumour tissue (block 3 was suggested) and POLE sequencing if feasible to establish the integrated molecular subgroup. **A stage- and molecular-specific adjuvant recommendation is not possible yet.** If final findings indicate low-risk uterine-confined disease, observation may suffice; higher-risk anatomical findings, substantial LVSI or a p53-abnormal profile may warrant radiotherapy and/or systemic therapy, while early-stage POLE-ultramutated disease may allow de-escalation. Decide adjuvant treatment at the tumour board using final stage and molecular results.",
