        "summary": "CRITICAL FLAGS / REVIEW POINTS\nNo morphologic–immunophenotypic discordance and no studies listed as pending. Specimen limitation: diagnostic biopsy (>15 fragments, 1–4 mm, one block) does not include muscularis propria, serosa/peritoneum, or lymph nodes, so the pT below is the invasion demonstrated in the sample and must be read with clinical/MRI stage. Tumour budding (ITBCC 2016) was not scored. LVI-negative applies only to the tissue examined. Margins are not a parameter of this unoriented biopsy.\n\nSPECIMEN\nLower rectum, diagnostic biopsy (req. 2605374; man, 62 years; reported 05/05/2026).\n\nAI ASSISTANT'S PRELIMINARY DIAGNOSIS\nLow-grade rectal adenocarcinoma, NOS (conventional; moderately differentiated), pMMR/MSS, HER2-negative (IHC 1+), pT1 pNX (AJCC 8th edition), with adjacent high-grade dysplasia.\n\nKEY FINDINGS\n- Grade: low-grade (WHO 5th edition two-tier; issued as moderately differentiated).\n- Stage: pT1 pNX (AJCC 8th). Submucosal invasion on the basis of invasive adenocarcinoma with significant desmoplasia; muscularis propria not sampled. M category is outside this specimen.\n- Margins: not applicable (unoriented diagnostic biopsy).\n- Invasion: desmoplastic invasive carcinoma, extensively ulcerated; lymphovascular invasion not identified. Perineural invasion not stated.\n- Markers (percentages not given): CK20+, CDX2+, SATB2+, CK7−; p53 overexpression (mutant pattern); HER2 1+; MLH1, MSH2, MSH6, and PMS2 retained.\n- Molecular (IHC-defined): pMMR/MSS; TP53-mutant pattern; HER2-negative. RAS/BRAF not reported.\n- Tumour budding: not scored (ITBCC 2016 Bd category not assigned).\n- Pending studies: none.\n\nINTERPRETATION\nInvasive gland-forming carcinoma with a significant desmoplastic reaction is submucosal invasion, distinct from the separately described high-grade crypt dysplasia in adjacent rectal mucosa. That pairing is a conventional dysplasia–carcinoma sequence primary, not intramucosal neoplasia alone and not a metastasis.\n\nWHO Classification of Tumours, 5th edition (Digestive System Tumours): adenocarcinoma, NOS. No mucinous, signet-ring, medullary, or serrated subtype is designated. Two-tier grading places the issued moderately differentiated carcinoma in the low-grade category (historical G2; gland-forming, not poorly differentiated). Ulceration and desmoplasia do not change grade.\n\nAJCC 8th edition, on the tissue examined: pT1 (through muscularis mucosae into submucosa; muscularis propria not represented, so pT2 or higher is not supported). No nodes were submitted: pNX. AJCC 8th has no pMX; distant metastasis is not a finding of this biopsy. Anatomic stage group is therefore pT1 pNX on this specimen.\n\nCK20/CDX2/SATB2 positive and CK7 negative is the rectal/colorectal immunophenotype and matches the labeled site. p53 overexpression is a mutant IHC pattern (missense-type surrogate) and, with retained MMR proteins and conventional histology, fits the chromosomal-instability pathway.\n\nMMR: nuclear MLH1, MSH2, MSH6, and PMS2 expressed in the usual manner. The report’s “low probability of microsatellite instability” is classified from that result as mismatch-repair proficient (pMMR), microsatellite-stable phenotype. This is not an MSI-high or Lynch-pattern carcinoma; MMR status does not support immune-checkpoint blockade.\n\nHER2, colorectal-specific criteria (basolateral/lateral membranous scoring; not breast criteria): IHC 1+ is negative. It is not equivocal (2+) and not positive (3+). Reflex ISH is not indicated, and the result does not meet colorectal criteria for HER2-targeted therapy.\n\nITBCC 2016 budding (invasive-front hotspot, 0.785 mm²: Bd1 = 0–4, Bd2 = 5–9, Bd3 ≥10) was not reported. A Bd category is not inferred from the absence of a count. Absent LVI is recorded as issued and is not upgraded by the fragmented sample.\n\nRECOMMENDED CORRELATIONS AND STUDIES\n- Correlate with pelvic MRI and staging CT before treatment; biopsy pT1 is not the clinical T category of a mass-forming lower rectal tumour.\n- Extended RAS (KRAS/NRAS) and BRAF V600E testing before any anti-EGFR decision; not addressed by the current IHC.\n- Score tumour budding on the existing slide by ITBCC 2016 if an invasive front is present.\n- HER2 ISH is not indicated for IHC 1+. MSI PCR and germline Lynch testing are not indicated from intact four-protein MMR IHC.\n- On any later excision specimen, synoptic AJCC reporting (mural depth, nodes, CRM, EMVI, budding) supersedes this biopsy pT1 pNX.",
