        "summary": "## CRITICAL FLAGS / REVIEW POINTS\nThe fragmented biopsy does not identify the deepest involved bowel-wall layer or provide an invasive-front tumour-budding count. **pT1 is a minimum, biopsy-based inference**, not evidence that invasion is confined to submucosa; margins and nodes are unsampled. The report's “p53 mutated” reflects an aberrant IHC pattern, not sequence-confirmed *TP53* mutation. Retained MMR staining establishes pMMR by IHC, not molecularly confirmed MSS. No studies are reported as pending.\n\n## SPECIMEN\nLower rectum tumour, biopsy (>15 fragments, one block; report 2605374, 5 May 2026).\n\n## AI ASSISTANT'S PRELIMINARY DIAGNOSIS\nInvasive conventional rectal adenocarcinoma, **WHO 5th-edition low grade (moderately differentiated)**; minimum **AJCC 8th-edition pT1**; pMMR and HER2-negative (IHC 1+).\n\n## KEY FINDINGS\n- **Invasion/grade:** Desmoplastic stromal response supports invasion; adjacent high-grade dysplasia. No lymphovascular invasion identified; perineural invasion not reported. Two-tier grade: **low**.\n- **Stage/margins:** **At least pT1** on biopsy; anatomic depth beyond the invasive component is not documented. pN and pM are unassigned because nodal and metastatic tissue were not submitted. Margins: not applicable to a diagnostic biopsy.\n- **Phenotype/biomarkers:** CK20+, CDX2+, SATB2+, CK7−; aberrant p53 overexpression. MLH1, MSH2, MSH6 and PMS2 retained (**pMMR; MSI-H unlikely by IHC**). **HER2 IHC 1+ = negative** by colorectal-specific scoring. No marker percentages are reported; molecular MSI and *KRAS/NRAS/BRAF* results are not reported.\n- **ITBCC 2016 budding:** Bd tier unreported; no bud count per **0.785 mm²** invasive-front hotspot is provided.\n\n## INTERPRETATION\nAdjacent high-grade dysplasia and the CK20+/CDX2+/SATB2+/CK7− profile support a rectal primary; desmoplasia supports invasive carcinoma rather than dysplasia alone. Moderate differentiation places this conventional adenocarcinoma in the WHO two-tier **low-grade** category. AJCC 8th-edition **pT1 is the minimum inferred invasive category**; the biopsy provides no basis to establish a deeper pT category or an overall stage group. Retained MMR proteins indicate pMMR with a low likelihood of MSI-H, while HER2 1+ is negative under colorectal criteria; p53 overexpression does not establish a sequenced mutation.\n\n## RECOMMENDED CORRELATIONS AND STUDIES\nCorrelate with endoscopy, pelvic MRI and clinical systemic staging for local extent and nodal/distant status. On adequately sampled invasive-front tissue, record ITBCC budding (**Bd1: 0–4; Bd2: 5–9; Bd3: ≥10 buds per 0.785 mm²**) and assess depth, LVI, PNI and margins as applicable. Obtain *KRAS/NRAS/BRAF* genotyping if systemic-therapy decisions warrant it; consider molecular MSI testing if clinically indicated or discordant with IHC.",
